nd":"1926-12-31","datePrecision":"range_approx","sortDate":"1925-12-01","sortOrder":13.6,"displayMode":"cluster","eventType":"career","period":"warsaw","periodKey":"warsaw","category":"professional_network","filterTags":["career","warsaw"],"placeDisplay":"Warsaw","cityKey":"warsaw","shortDescription":"Kaper later traced his entry into popular song to a Warsaw network linking “Henry Craig,” Andrzej Włast, cabaret performance, and Altschuler’s publishing house.","longDescription":"Kaper’s own account presents the move into songwriting as accidental: a friend whom he called “Henry Craig” introduced him to a leading Warsaw lyricist identifiable as Andrzej Włast, after which the song reached the cabaret stage and then print. Read together with the surviving printed songs, this episode explains how a composer trained in concert idioms entered the commercial structures of interwar Warsaw popular song: lyricist, cabaret performer, publisher, and sheet-music circulation.","featured":true,"roles":["career_milestone","professional_network","publication_event","career_mechanism"],"personIds":["P003","P009","P119"],"sourceIds":["SRC0053","SRC0054","SRC0055","SRC0490"],"workIds":["W-S002","W-S005","W-S006"],"mediaIds":["M035","M067","M125","M126","M206"],"heroMediaIds":["M067"],"placeIds":["PL001"],"periods":["warsaw"]}],"places":[{"id":"PL001","displayName":"Warsaw","authorizedName":"Warsaw / Warszawa","placeType":"city","city":"Warsaw","region":"Masovian Voivodeship","country":"Poland","latitude":52.229676,"longitude":21.012229,"period":"warsaw","slug":"warsaw","publicNote":"Kaper’s birthplace and the main city of his education and early musical activity before his move to Berlin.","mapPrecision":"city_level","publicScope":"map_and_detail","timelineEventIds":["TE0001","TE0002","TE0003","TE0004","TE0005","TE0006","TE0008","TE0009","TE0011","TE0012","TE0013","TE0014","TE0015","TE0020","TE0044","TE0045","TE0046","TE0047"],"mediaIds":["M097"],"sourceIds":["SRC0012","SRC0490"],"peri